JavaScript hoisting means that before code execution starts, JavaScript creates memory for variable and function declarations.
During this memory creation phase, function declarations are fully initialized, var variables are initialized with undefined, and let/const are hoisted but left uninitialized.
After memory creation, the code is executed line by line.

